   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 38108305,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 1989064,
    "poster_id": 212018,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\"  width=\"42\" height=\"13\" > be an acute triangle with circumcircle <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" >.</span> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" > be the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" > and suppose that <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/f/e6f7d674f6a3b126bb50cf825075af8238b4fb95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|AD|=|BC|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" >.</span><br>\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" > be the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" > on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" > and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" > be the intersection of the angular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/8/c28b8d709d3b873ec6db017839b1520919db39db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" > with <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\"  width=\"27\" height=\"13\" >.</span><br>\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68a18a29a2c5e1076bca9efe1bdb8e9003bf590b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y \\ne B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" > be a point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" > such that <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/c/68c9bac619bb5e627241e5aee06e6f30d3a7d76e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BY \\parallel AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" >.</span> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\"  width=\"30\" height=\"12\" > intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" > again in <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/243ffa8dc7b01e076fb03c7596b6c50184668ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z \\ne Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" >.</span><br>\nFinally, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/b/bbbf24a758576d16eac9027bca6f957f490bd778.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\ne W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" > be the second intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\"  width=\"27\" height=\"13\" > with the circumcircle of <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/1/ec106927a80d0092b58132805d34caaad3c6b0bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YWZ$\"  width=\"48\" height=\"12\" >.</span> Show that <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/7/037e9fed857548e3a54a46d24fcc36eac20b8021.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DZS=90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" >.</span>",
    "post_canonical": "Let $ABC$ be an acute triangle with circumcircle $k$. Let $D$ be the foot of the altitude from $A$ and suppose that $|AD|=|BC|$.\nLet $X$ be the foot of the altitude from $D$ on $AB$ and let $W$ be the intersection of the angular bisector of $\\angle ADC$ with $AC$.\nLet $Y \\ne B$ be a point on $k$ such that $BY \\parallel AC$. Let $XY$ intersect $k$ again in $Z \\ne Y$.\nFinally, let $S \\ne W$ be the second intersection of $AC$ with the circumcircle of $YWZ$. Show that $\\angle DZS=90^\\circ$.",
    "username": "Tintarn",
